                {
                  "formattedValue": "Test Ability to Catch Invalid Solutions (False positives) "
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "\"False positive:\nThe suite is superficial because it tests only the happy path and ignores many explicit workflow rules. It never validates student/course existence, status-transition correctness, or rejected/approved grading constraints, allowing fundamentally broken registration logic to pass. Pending-list filtering, duplicate approvals, invalid statuses, and persistence rules are completely untested, so many incorrect implementations would still succeed.\n\"\n\nThe tests exercise only the happy path two trades created and basic external_id checks while ignoring critical behaviors like retry logic, error handling, duplicate prevention, order linking, symbol filtering, and correct field mapping. None of the expanded trade fields (side, price, amount, fee, fee_token, order_external_id) are validated. As a result, many severely broken implementations would still pass, making the suite highly permissive."
                },
