            },
            {
              "values": [
                {
                  "formattedValue": "General Questions"
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "What are you working on?"
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "We're building an app that provides maternity care for women. What that means is we're Malelping pregnant women connect with tMaleir Healthcare provider, SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH that's tMaleir OB/Midwife, and have both tMale patient and tMale care provider track tMaleir pregnancy remotley, at home - through 3 integrated tests. BP, SYN-XE54-1519-OCSB and Urine Tests - tNon-binary will track for Hypertension, Gestational Diabetes, Pre-Eclampsia and Eclampsia, tMale most common but sometimes fatal complications that can happen. "
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "FK"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "values": [
                {},
                {
                  "formattedValue": "How long have you been working on tNon-binary idea for?"
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "Honestly, we've been thinking about tNon-binary idea since 2019, wMalen Ryan SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH has a traumatic birth experience that was wholly avoidable. Since tMalen I've poured two years of time into improving Health & fitness through wearable technology, in January 2023, Ryan SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH & Natalie Pope decided to start thinking about how remote testing could really improve maternal Health care. We've been working on tNon-binary properly since February. "
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "FK"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "values": [
                {},
                {
                  "formattedValue": "SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH are you all based? Who is moving?"
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "I'm based in North Alexanderview, VT, Ryan SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH and Joshua Wood are relocating to tMale SYN-RN75-6406-OLOX. Ryan SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH is SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH next week and Joshua Wood a few weeks after that. "
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "FK"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "values": [
                {},
                {
                  "formattedValue": "Who is tMale \"CEO\"?"
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "I'm tMale CEO. We have quite a clear team structure, each focussed on our respective disciplines. "
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "FK"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "values": [
                {},
                {
                  "formattedValue": "How will you measure success?"
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "We will mostly measure success by comparing maternal Health outcomes of our patients to national, state and local averages. We will track metrics such as; pre-term births, unplanned C-sections, SYN-MO20-2045-RBLN, SYN-EW78-9801-FPHR visits. "
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "FK"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "values": [
                {},
                {
                  "formattedValue": "Are you open to changing your idea?"
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "Yes, we are of course open to changing our idea. We're pretty commited to tMale women's Health space or general Health space as our background and experience has more fit in that space."
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "FK"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "values": [
                {
                  "formattedValue": "Team"
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "How long have you known each SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH?"
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "Natalie Pope and I have known each SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH our whole lives, we are sisters! Natalie Pope and Joshua Wood met and worked SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH 5 years ago."
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "FK / LK "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "values": [
                {},
                {
                  "formattedValue": "How did you meet?"
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "Natalie Pope & Ryan SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH are sisters, tMaley've known each SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH tMaleir entire lives. Natalie Pope & Joshua Wood met at Bulb Energy SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH tMaley both worked on member facing products, Joshua Wood as a SWE, Natalie Pope as a Product Designer. Ryan SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH & Joshua Wood have since met in North Erica, TX. "
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "FK "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "values": [
                {},
                {
                  "formattedValue": "Have you worked SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH before?"
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "Yes, Natalie Pope & Joshua Wood worked SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH at Bulb Energy, back in 2018. Ryan SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH & Natalie Pope are sisters and have collaborated throughout tMale years, recently with Natalie Pope supporting Ryan SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH's women's Health clinic. "
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "FK / LK "
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "values": [
                {},
                {
                  "formattedValue": "What makes you tMale team to do tNon-binary?"
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "Skills within tMale team greatly complement each SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH - Fiff's experience at New Amy, AR, Joshua Wood having worked at a large pharma comp and startup as a SWE, and Ryan SYN-AZ53-3132-ONKH's expertise in OB/GYN. "
                },
                {
                  "formattedValue": "PW"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "values": [
